1. WHAT THIS FILE IS

This file is the copyright notice and the statement of terms for this repository, and it is
the file a reader, a judge or an employer should open first when asking what may be done with
the work here. It is plain text so that it reads the same in an editor, in a browser and in a
diff.

It is not a grant of rights. No outbound licence has been chosen for this repository yet; that
decision is the copyright holder's and it is still open. When it is made, section 2 below is
replaced in full and this file becomes the chosen licence's own text. Nothing else in this
file changes when that happens, because sections 3 and 4 are not the holder's to give away.


2. THE TERMS TODAY

The work in this repository is Copyright (c) 2026 Nayil Arana, all rights reserved.

Reading this repository is not restricted by this file. The restrictions below concern copying
and use, and they are what the default of copyright already says:

  - No copy of this work, in whole or in part, may be redistributed, published, sold, rented,
    sublicensed or included in another work.
  - No modified version, port, translation, asset extraction or other derivative work may be
    made or distributed.
  - No part of this work may be used commercially, including its code, its art, its music, its
    sound effects, its text or its data tables.
  - The name Primordial Paradox and the names of its characters may not be used to endorse or
    promote anything.

A written licence from the copyright holder is the only thing that changes any of the above.
Asking is welcome; assuming is not.


3. THIRD PARTY MATERIAL THIS FILE CANNOT SPEAK FOR

Nothing in section 2 narrows a third party's rights, and nothing in this file grants what a
third party owns. Four things in this repository are not the holder's alone, and each is
recorded with its required line in CREDITS.md:

  - Engine. GameMaker LTS2026, by YoYo Games Ltd, used under YoYo Games' own licence. The
    engine is not distributed in this repository.

  - Font. Press Start 2P, Copyright 2012 The Press Start 2P Project Authors
    (cody@zone38.net), with Reserved Font Name "Press Start 2P", under the SIL Open Font
    License 1.1. The licence text as published upstream is kept byte for byte at
    knowledge/licences/PressStart2P-OFL.txt, and the same text is carried inside the build in
    data/credits.json so that the notice travels with the game rather than only with the
    repository. The glyphs rasterised into this game's own sprite sheets are use of the font,
    not a modified font, and the Reserved Font Name is not used for anything else.

  - Map data. The street geometry was derived from OpenStreetMap data under the Open Database
    Licence 1.0. The required line, exactly as this repository writes it everywhere else:

    (c) OpenStreetMap contributors, Open Database Licence (ODbL) 1.0, https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright

  - Everything else. The GML code, the art, the music, the sound effects, the dialogue, the
    names and the data tables in this repository were made for this project. No third party
    library is imported: the ten libraries that were read and approved are recorded in
    knowledge/LICENSES.md and none of their code is in this tree.


4. WHAT AN OUTBOUND LICENCE WOULD CHANGE, AND WHAT IT WOULD NOT

An outbound licence would replace section 2 with its own terms, and it could be permissive or
narrow, MIT or Apache 2.0 or something else again. It would not touch section 3. A grant made
here cannot grant what this project does not own: the engine, the font and the map data stay
under their own licences, and a redistributor of this game inherits those obligations along
with the game.

The two licences this project already accepts for code it takes in (MIT and Apache 2.0, see
knowledge/LICENSES.md) are also the two an outbound grant would most naturally use, but the
choice is the holder's and is not made here.


5. WHERE THE OBLIGATIONS ARE RECORDED

  - CREDITS.md, at the root beside this file: one row per attribution obligation, with the
    exact line each licence requires and the place in the build where that line travels.
  - knowledge/LICENSES.md: every library that was read, its header verbatim, its licence, and
    what may be reused from it. Nothing enters this project without a row there.
  - knowledge/PROVENANCE.md: what was studied, what was never copied, and the clean room
    checks that hold that claim on every commit.
  - data/credits.json: the one screen the game shows, plus the full text of the notices that
    have to travel inside the build.


6. STATUS OF THE OPEN DECISION

Recorded 2026-10-23. No outbound licence has been chosen. This file therefore states the
default position, all rights reserved, which is what the absence of a grant means. The
holder's decision, when it is made, is one edit to section 2 of this file plus the matching
paragraph in README.md, and it is his to make.
